# First-party SHACL Rules case: a RUN-ONCE rule inside a later layer.
#
# SHACL 1.2 Inference Rules executes "For all layers in the rule set (in ascending
# order): […] Execute one iteration over all run-once rules in the layer; do
# Execute one iteration over all iterating rules in the layer while the iteration
# has produced newly inferred triples".
#
#   sh:layer 0 — an iterating sh:TripleRule typing every ex:Employee as an ex:Person.
#   sh:layer 1 — a run-once (sh:runOnce true) sh:SPARQLRule whose CONSTRUCT template
#                carries a blank node, minting one address resource per ex:Person.
#
# The run-once rule runs at the start of ITS layer, not of the run. Because layer 0
# is complete first, `ex:alice rdf:type ex:Person` already holds when layer 1
# resolves its sh:targetClass focus nodes, so the mint fires for ex:alice. A
# scheduler that hoisted every run-once rule to the start of the whole run would
# find no ex:Person at all and derive nothing here.
#
# Exactly ONE address blank is minted per focus node: the rule is not re-evaluated
# after its single firing.

@prefix ex:  <http://example.org/ns#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix sh:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

ex:alice rdf:type ex:Employee .

ex:TypeRule
  rdf:type sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetClass ex:Employee ;
  sh:rule [
      rdf:type sh:TripleRule ;
      sh:layer 0 ;
      sh:subject sh:this ;
      sh:predicate rdf:type ;
      sh:object ex:Person ] .

ex:AddrRule
  rdf:type sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetClass ex:Person ;
  sh:rule [
      rdf:type sh:SPARQLRule ;
      sh:layer 1 ;
      sh:runOnce true ;
      sh:construct """CONSTRUCT { $this ex:addr _:a . _:a ex:city ex:Metropolis . }
                      WHERE { $this a ex:Person }""" ] .
